{"name":"Honeycomb","hex":"#ddaa11","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Honeycomb","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Honeycomb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honeycomb","blocks":[{"text":"A honeycomb is a mass of hexagonal prismatic cells built from beeswax by honey bees in their nests to contain their brood and stores of honey and pollen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Honey_comb.jpg/330px-Honey_comb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeycomb","wikidata":"Q123339"},{"title":"Honeycomb (geometry)","blocks":[{"text":"In geometry, a honeycomb is a space filling or close packing of polyhedral or higher-dimensional cells, so that there are no gaps. It is an example of the more general mathematical tiling or tessellation in any number of dimensions. Its dimension can be clarified as n-honeycomb for a honeycomb of n-dimensional space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Cubic_honeycomb.png/330px-Cubic_honeycomb.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeycomb_(geometry)","wikidata":"Q1189295"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg/500px-Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg/1280px-Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Honeyco